# The map with tiles under it: a pack read off the card, one tile per frame.
#
# What this scene is a picture of is the *filling*, which is the whole of the decision behind it.
# A cold tile costs 2-5 ms on the Brick's card and a view stands on about twenty of them, so
# drawing a full panel in one pass would be a tenth of a second in which the BLE link goes
# unread - on a client that is one epoll loop, that is not a slow map, it is a client that stops.
# One tile a frame fills the same view in about twenty frames with input serviced between each,
# and that is what the frames after every press below are.
#
# The pack is named rather than found: a scene that picked up whatever pack the developer had
# installed would render differently on two machines. It is drawn rather than downloaded, so
# nothing here is anybody else's pixels - `make demo-pack` writes it, and docs/ui.md says what
# that is for.
#
# The graticule is still under the tiles and is not replaced by them, which is what the holes at
# the pack's edge and the seconds before a tile arrives are drawn as. Pan far enough and the
# pictures run out and the grid is all there is, which is the honest picture of a regional pack.

scene demo
map pack build/demo.mctp
waypoint ALFA Ridge repeater | up the fire road, gate code is on the tag

# Into the map from the first row of the Nodes list, which is where it is opened from.
tab nodes
hold 800
key a
hold 2000

# A direction stops on the next marker that way, so the view re-centres and the tiles under the
# new middle are fetched from there outwards - the nearest to the crosshair first, because that
# is where the reader is looking.
key left
hold 1800

# One level closer. Every tile in view is a different tile at a different zoom, so this is the
# fill loop's real workload rather than a pan's edge row.
key x
hold 2000

# And back out twice, to where the pack's own edge is on the panel: the streets stop and the
# graticule carries on, which is what a pack of one region looks like from far enough away.
key y
hold 1200
key y
hold 2400
